Cell["\<\
Answer: the ranks are 1, 1, 0, 0, 2, 3. For b = -82 the three generators (-1, \
9), (-8, 12), (-9, 3) have small x, so a search bound of 10 is enough (the \
default bound 50 takes over ten minutes). For b = 73 the two points found \
equal the proven bound 2, and for b = -82 the three points equal the proven \
bound 3, so these ranks are proved. For b = 7 and 17, ECPRankBound only gives \
2; the analytic rank (or a full 2-descent) gives 0. For b = 17 the 2-descent \
itself cannot decide, because the Tate-Shafarevich group has elements of \
order 2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5c51d48-87b2-4f90-9dd3-ddc2b8bd1632"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

